<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="TolE0107">
<l>uyiriṟu coṉmu ṉuyirvaru vaḻiyu</l>
<l>muyiriṟu coṉmuṉ meyvaru vaḻiyu</l>
<l>meyyiṟu coṉmu ṉuyirvaru vaḻiyu</l>
<l>meyyiṟu coṉmuṉ meyvaru vaḻiyumeṉ</l>
<l>ṟivveṉa vaṟiyak kiḷakkuṅ kālai</l>
<l>niṟutta collē kuṟittuvaru kiḷaviyeṉ</l>
<l>ṟāyī riyala puṇarnilaic cuṭṭē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
<l>When [one] defines [rules] in the combination [of sounds]<note place="foot"><foreign xml:lang="ta">puṇarnilai.</foreign></note></l>
<l>which are concerned with those two-</l>
<l>the standing word<note place="foot"><foreign xml:lang="ta">nivutta col.</foreign></note> and the particular coming word-<note place="foot"><foreign xml:lang="ta">kuṟittu varu kiḷavi.</foreign></note></l>
<l>one should know these as such [which may be classified as]</l>
<l>when vowel follows a vowel-ending,</l>
<l>when consonant follows a vowel-ending,</l>
<l>when vowel follows a consonant-ending</l>
<l>[and] when consonant follows a consonant-ending.</l>
      </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
